30.
Land in which hereditary rights shall not accrue
. - Notwithstanding anything in Section 29, hereditary rights shall not accrue in, -
(1)
grove-land, pasture land, or land covered by water and used for the purpose of growing singhara or other produce;
(2)
land used for the casual or occasional cultivation in the bed of a river;
(3)
land acquired or held for a public purpose or a work of public utility; and in particular, and without prejudice to the
generality of this clause, -
(a)
